module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_launch_argv_names_a_credential_snapshot_no_take_wrote

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { CeilingNotStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_launch_argv_names_a_credential_snapshot_no_take_wrote: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_launch_argv_names_a_credential_snapshot_no_take_wrote" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: CeilingNotStated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a Claude or Cursor launch argv names the attempt's credential snapshot path while no take wrote a snapshot there. The argv builders (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dispatch_actuator claude_inner_argv_for_credential, gunbc.cursor_harness_credential cursor_worker_turn_argv) took the path as a NonEmptyStr, and the spawn fold re-derived it from the attempt identity (then dispatch_credential_snapshot_path_for_instance), so an argv for a written snapshot and an argv for an unwritten one were identical values.",
    "HARM: the spawn stages a worktree, attempt state and a session or unit, and only then does the child's wrapper exit 78 on the missing file -- a launch the dispatcher could have refused before staging anything. Specimens on main: the instance-less fold dispatch_provider_inner_argv built a Claude argv with no credential at all, and the uncalled dispatch_spawn_commands_for_inventory Claude arm built one for a snapshot no selection had taken.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the path is the IDENTITY of where a take writes, and stays derived from the attempt identity; what was missing is the PROOF that the take ran. Recomputing the path at the spawn was deliberate (selection and spawn derive the same path), and it is exactly what let the proof go uncarried. The converse holds too: a proof of take is not a proof of THIS attempt's take. Carried alone, a snapshot from one selection could license another attempt's, provider's or instance's launch, which the re-derived path never could -- the first form of this repair carried the proof and dropped that binding, and review caught it. The second form recorded the subject and compared it at the spawn fold and at the discard -- a runtime refusal every launch leg had to remember, because the spawn still received the attempt beside the snapshot. The third form (this one) removes the second attempt: the belt names the attempt it owns, preparation acquires for it, and the launch legs read the attempt from the sealed prepared launch, so there is nothing for them to compare.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (the child's wrapper exits 78 after staging). RUNG NOW: structurally guaranteed at the launch boundary on the routes that check sole_constructor and admit_callers. gunbc.dispatch_credential_snapshot TakenCredentialSnapshot is sole_constructor in a file holding only the take, and records the attempt (gunbc.dispatch_attempt DispatchAttempt) and the executor it was taken for. Every launch leg -- the spawn plan (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dispatch_actuator dispatch_spawn_commands_for_launch), the provider argv (dispatch_provider_inner_argv_for_launch), the belt's staging and placement (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate belt_spawn_addressing) and its discard (belt_snapshot_owned_outcome) -- consumes the sealed prepared launch (gunbc.dispatch_attempt_launch PreparedAttemptLaunch) and reads the attempt, the executor and the snapshot from it; the standing probes come earlier, borrowing the TakenCredentialSnapshot itself before the prepared launch is minted, so a Claude or Cursor launch with no snapshot, a Codex or harness launch holding one, and a launch pairing one attempt's snapshot with another attempt's worktree have no expression there. The prepared launch has one mint (prepare_attempt_launch), admit_callers-confined to the one producer every draw goes through (attempt_selection_launching), which joins the two independent inputs once: the executor the selection resolved must be the launch's, and the launch's attempt must be the one the belt requested -- an unrelated snapshot refuses rather than relabelling the requested work. Witnessed by test.claim.dispatch_credential_snapshot_seal_witness (forged snapshot literal, cast and nested spellings, a forged prepared launch, and a foreign call to the mint each refuse; a lawful carry into a launch does not) and test.claim.dispatch_credential_snapshot_wet_witness (the launch names the snapshot the real take wrote for it, and replacing the custody file after the take changes nothing it reads; a launch prepared for another attempt, another instance, or under another executor's selection refuses at the join).",
    "RESIDUALS, EACH WITH THE CAPABILITY THAT CLOSES IT: (1) native v2 checks sole_constructor (v2.compiler.infer infer_sole_constructor_diags); the seed still misses coproduct-variant and parameter-default construction (f13/f19), which is why the seal is on the outer records and not on the AttemptLaunch alternatives. (2) The seal proves the write succeeded when the take ran, not that the bytes are present at exec -- the wrapper's exit 78 remains the mitigation for a file removed in between; the ceiling for that is outside the modeled guarantee (another process may unlink it). (3) The take now joins the custody bytes to a root-published export receipt (gunbc.host_custody_export_receipt, required, no receipt-free fallback) and records JoinedCustodyGeneration on the sealed snapshot. RUNG NOW for the source: mechanically preventable on the executed take. What stays residual: receipt.host is joined to SnapshotCustodyDeclaration.host (same HostIdentity). The instance's host is an unbranded dashboard NonEmptyStr; the Cursor draw compares it to the declaration host by string, and the take does not observe the execution host. The writer's pairing remains one call site (plan_host_custody_export). Closes the remaining host residual when those identities are one type and the take observes the execution host; closes the writer residual when a sealed fetch result carries version and payload together. (4) The attempt's identity is joined once, at the mint; the belt's own steps before selection (footprint and environment admission) use the instance and node it was given, and the steps after it read them from the prepared launch. (5) The attempt names its instance's host; that the take ran on that host is not recorded -- a take on another host still reaches the child's exit 78, as before this change. (6) The snapshot's lifetime is not yet owned: nothing refuses an escape of the handle, and an acquisition whose owner dies before the attempt is recorded is not recovered -- closes with an acquisition registered before its bytes are written and recovered by a surviving owner, and with an ownership rule on the acquired instance.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.dispatch_credential_snapshot_seal_witness", decl_name: "a_forged_snapshot_literal_is_refused_at_compile", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.dispatch_credential_snapshot_wet_witness", decl_name: "a_cursor_turn_on_srv2_binds_the_taken_snapshot_through_the_env_wrapper", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.dispatch_credential_snapshot_seal_witness", decl_name: "a_forged_prepared_launch_is_refused_at_compile", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.dispatch_credential_snapshot_wet_witness", decl_name: "a_launch_prepared_for_another_attempt_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.dispatch_credential_snapshot_wet_witness", decl_name: "a_cursor_selection_holding_a_claude_snapshot_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.dispatch_credential_snapshot_wet_witness", decl_name: "replacing_the_custody_file_after_the_take_does_not_change_the_launch_input", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
